// E0200: an integer is not a pointer. `const p: i32* = 42;` always said so;
// the same store through `=` did not, because assignment asks a second question
// after `can_assign` says no - whether one level of pointer/reference SPELLING
// separates two otherwise-assignable types. That question peeled `i32*` to
// `i32`, compared it against the `i64` literal, found them castable, and waived
// the diagnosis. Cryo has no implicit integer<->pointer conversion in either
// direction; the address has to be written with `as`.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0200)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::AssignIntToPointer;
function main() -> int {
    mut p: i32* = null;
    p = 42;   //~ ERROR[E0200] mismatched types
    return 0;
}
